{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the bariatric team doctors. You came in tonight because of low blood sugar—can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up this morning feeling really shaky and confused. My glucose monitor alarm went off—it said my blood sugar was 43."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s quite low. Did you treat it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I took my sugar pills right away. I felt better after a few minutes, but then it happened again later today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. We’re going to keep an eye on your levels. You also mentioned increased drainage around your G-tube and some pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:20:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the site has been leaking more than usual. I’m changing the dressing twice a day now because it gets soaked. And it’s tender—more than normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check that. We’ve ordered a scan to make sure your tube is still in the right place and not leaking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it possible the feeds are backing up into the bag? I’ve been worried the pump isn’t delivering them properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-02-18 20:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good question. The scan will help us see how the contrast moves. If it’s refluxing, we’ll adjust your setup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your abdominal X-ray with contrast shows the G-tube is correctly placed in the stomach. No leakage outside the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the tube is okay? But why am I having these lows?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tube is working, but we think your hypoglycemia might be related to bacterial overgrowth in your intestines. You’ve had that before, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, from my breath test. So that could be causing the lows?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Bacteria can ferment carbs and trigger insulin release. We’re restarting your Flagyl to treat it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about the soreness at the tube site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed some granulation tissue—extra tissue that sometimes grows around tubes. It can cause irritation and drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:38:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-02-18 22:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s common. We’ll treat it with silver nitrate to reduce it and prescribe an ointment called Bactroban to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugars have been stable overnight—between 80 and 110. No episodes of hypoglycemia so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does that mean the Flagyl is working already?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s early, but staying on your feeds and being in a controlled setting helps. Your endocrinologist wants a fasting test to check what’s driving the insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A fasting test? But I need my tube feeds to avoid lows."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do it carefully. We’ll stop the feeds and monitor your blood sugar every hour. When it drops to around 55, we’ll draw blood to check insulin, C-peptide, and other levels, then restart your feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And that will tell us why I’m having lows?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-02-19 08:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. It helps distinguish if it’s from too much insulin production, reactive hypoglycemia, or something else. Your endocrinologist will review the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did the fasting test this morning. You went about 12 hours without feeds. Your blood sugar dropped to 55, and we got the labs right then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How did I do? Did I pass out or anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you stayed alert the whole time. Nurses checked you every hour. All the labs were sent to your endocrinologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And the contrast study this morning—what did that show?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The contrast moved all the way into your colon and rectum. That means your digestive tract is open and functioning—no blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So everything’s moving like it should?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-02-19 14:37:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And your tube site is looking better after treatment. We’ll keep using the silver nitrate and Bactroban ointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. Another good night—your sugars stayed between 55 and 110. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What will I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue your tube feeds as before. Take Flagyl three times a day for the bacterial overgrowth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the new meds—octreotide and acarbose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Octreotide helps reduce insulin spikes, and acarbose slows sugar absorption. They may help prevent lows after meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And for the tube site?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Apply the Bactroban ointment twice a day to the granulation tissue. Keep the dressing clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I have my follow-up with Dr. ___?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-02-20 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll review your test results and adjust your plan if needed. We’ll send them all the labs from the fasting test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well—vitals stable, sugars in range. We’re ready to discharge you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any last instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking all your meds as prescribed. Use glucose tablets if your sugar drops. And call if you have fever, redness, or increased pain at the tube site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel shaky again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Check your sugar. If it’s low, treat it with glucose and sit down. If it doesn’t improve, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I feel much better knowing we’re on top of this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-02-21 07:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll send prescriptions for Flagyl, Bactroban, and the new meds. You’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-02-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just one more thing—should I keep checking my blood sugar at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-02-21 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially before meals and at bedtime. And any time you feel shaky or confused."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-02-21 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-02-21 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-02-18 19:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-02-21 09:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted due to recurrent hypoglycemia with a blood glucose of 43, accompanied by increased drainage and pain at her G-tube site. Imaging confirmed the G-tube was correctly positioned with no leakage, and contrast passed normally into the colon. She was restarted on metronidazole for small intestinal bacterial overgrowth, which may contribute to hypoglycemia. Granulation tissue at the G-tube site was treated with silver nitrate and mupirocin ointment. A fasting hypoglycemia work-up was completed, with labs drawn during a monitored fast before resuming feeds. She remained stable with blood glucose levels between 55 and 110, and was discharged home with new medications including octreotide and acarbose, instructions for wound care, and follow-up with her endocrinologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption",
      "Other specified disorders of intestine",
      "Other abnormal granulation tissue",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Body Mass Index 29.0-29.9, adult",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
